<title>UK: BOC completes US air separation plant.</title>
<headline>BOC completes US air separation plant.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British industrial gases firm BOC Group Plc said on Wednesday it had completed construction and commissioning of a large cryogenic air separation plant in western Pennsylvania.</p>
<p>BOC said it had invested more than $70 million in the plant, which had begun supplying oxygen to USX Corp's US Steel integrated steelworks in Pennsylvania's Monongahela Valley.</p>
<p>The plant has the capacity to produce more than 2,800 tons per day of oxygen, nitrogen and argon.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
